```

Order of defers: the recover defer is registered before the close defer → close runs first. But the test requires Defrob to be called before Close. So register the recover defer after the close defer? No — defers run in LIFO order. If I register close first and recover second, recover runs first, then close. That's what I want.

```go
defer func() { r.Close() }()
defer func() { recover handling }()
```

LIFO: recover defer (registered second) runs first → Defrob, then Close.

About err = p: p is an interface{} (any). The test checks err.Error() — p implements error. Since err is a named return value of type error, the assignment works.

TransientError check: the test returns TransientError directly (not wrapped), so a type assertion would also work, but errors.As is more robust. Use errors.As.

